            <ArticleTitle>A minimal multiconfigurational technique.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>201-207</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/jcc.540070213</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A direct minimization method previously presented by the authors is applied here to biconfigurational wave functions. A very moderate increasing in the time by iteration with respect to the one-determinant calculation and good convergence properties have been found. So qualitatively correct studies on singlet systems with strong biradical character can be performed with a cost similar to that required by Hartree-Fock calculations.</AbstractText>
